# Signing certificates, stored encrypted in a repository of their own.
#
# ## Why `match` and not "download the profile from the portal"
#
# Because the portal's answer changes. A profile regenerated by hand on one
# machine is a profile the CI has never seen, and the failure arrives at the
# worst moment — on a release, with an error that names a UUID rather than a
# cause. `match` makes the certificate a **versioned artefact**: the same bytes
# on the laptop and on the runner, restored from git, encrypted at rest.
#
# ⚠️ The repository is **dedicated to the portfolio**. Reusing another project's
# certificates repository would tie two release cycles together, and the scope
# rule refuses it — see `.claude/rules/scope-isolation.md`.

git_url(ENV["MATCH_GIT_URL"] || "https://github.com/Boris-David/portfolio-certificates")
storage_mode("git")
type("appstore")
app_identifier(["dev.amissan.portfolio"])
team_id("R55L6Z8K6R")

# CI must never be able to create or revoke a certificate: a runner that can
# regenerate signing material is a runner that can invalidate every other
# machine's. It reads, or it fails.
readonly(ENV["CI"] == "true")
